CPU=======RAM
GPU VRAM (close to GPU, fast, small)

PyTorch: a ML/AI framework, which build, train, run models
model server：a software application whose job is to run AI models and make them available to other applications

                     Model Server
                   ┌─────────────┐
Client ──request──→│ AI Model    │
                   │    ↓        │
                   │   GPU       │
                   │    ↓        │
Client ←─response──│ prediction  │
                   └─────────────┘


vLLM: a model server specificly for LLM; built on top of PyTorch, it wraps the model into a service with a normal web API
For example, if you have a Qwen or Llama model and want other applications to access it through an API, you can use vLLM.
Client / Application
        │
        │ API request
        ↓
      vLLM
        │
        ↓
    LLM Model
        │
        ↓
       GPU
        │
        ↓
   Generated Text
        │
        ↓
      Client
